00:08:42,660 --> 00:08:45,428
<i>in the way</i>
<i>only loving parents can do.</i>

239
00:08:45,544 --> 00:08:46,341
Whoop.

240
00:08:46,432 --> 00:08:47,431
Knock it off.

241
00:08:47,579 --> 00:08:48,483
Whoop.

242
00:08:48,594 --> 00:08:49,383
(Honks)

243
00:08:49,518 --> 00:08:50,481
Whoop.
(Honks)

244
00:08:50,598 --> 00:08:52,121
Whoop.
(Honks)

245
00:08:52,808 --> 00:08:53,435
Whoop.

246
00:08:53,548 --> 00:08:54,456
Stop it!

247
00:08:54,528 --> 00:08:55,718
Stop it, stop it,
stop it, stop it,

248
00:08:55,819 --> 00:08:56,749
stop it, stop it, stop it!

249
00:08:58,533 --> 00:09:00,922
Look, Brick,
we got you a bunny.

250
00:09:01,127 --> 00:09:02,301
Why?

251
00:09:03,229 --> 00:09:04,901
Oh, no reason.

252
00:09:05,192 --> 00:09:06,185
(High-pitched voice)
Whoop.

253
00:09:06,455 --> 00:09:07,349
(Thud)

254
00:09:08,515 --> 00:09:09,297
(Gasps)

255
00:09:09,400 --> 00:09:12,505
Oh... my... God.
You got us a bunny?!

256
00:09:12,642 --> 00:09:16,608
Aah! I can't <i>believe</i> it!

257
00:09:16,731 --> 00:09:17,966
Whoo!

258
00:09:18,072 --> 00:09:20,008
- What are you doing?
- I'm practicing.

259
00:09:20,119 --> 00:09:23,030
As a mascot, I have to
exaggerate all of my movements.

260
00:09:23,192 --> 00:09:28,918
I just <i>love</i> him <i>so much.</i>

261
00:09:29,639 --> 00:09:31,095
I thought we were
getting something smaller.

262
00:09:31,250 --> 00:09:32,706
(Sighs) We were, but they were
out of gerbils,

263
00:09:32,818 --> 00:09:34,053
and I didn't want to go back.

264
00:09:34,147 --> 00:09:36,020
Sue, get away from the bunny.
It's Brick's bunny.

265
00:09:36,171 --> 00:09:37,487
How come Brick gets a bunny?

266
00:09:37,663 --> 00:09:39,157
Because he's the youngest,

267
00:09:39,293 --> 00:09:40,546
and there are things
you got that he didn't,

268
00:09:40,660 --> 00:09:41,811
and now we've even.

269
00:09:41,970 --> 00:09:43,165
No, she can have it.

270
00:09:43,275 --> 00:09:46,039
(Gasps) Thank you
so much, Brick.

271
00:09:46,172 --> 00:09:48,498
Oh! He is so cute!

272
00:09:48,613 --> 00:09:50,778
I just love him so, so much!

273
00:09:50,934 --> 00:09:52,390
(Gasps)
I'm gonna name him "Bugs."

274
00:09:52,566 --> 00:09:54,427
No, you're not
naming it "Bugs."

275
00:09:54,567 --> 00:09:56,373
It's Brick's bunny.
He's gonna name him.

276
00:09:56,528 --> 00:09:57,543
"Bugs" is fine.

277
00:09:57,689 --> 00:09:59,406
Look! Look!
They got Brick a bunny.

278
00:09:59,547 --> 00:10:01,560
What? How come he gets
a bunny and I don't?

279
00:10:01,724 --> 00:10:03,401
(Lowered voice) 'Cause Brick
needs help and you don't,

280
00:10:03,507 --> 00:10:04,546
so Brick gets a bunny!

281
00:10:04,669 --> 00:10:06,363
Oh, so he does
weird stuff and gets things?

282
00:10:06,489 --> 00:10:07,551
I can do weird stuff.

283
00:10:07,678 --> 00:10:10,759
Ooh! Aah! Blah-huh-hoo! Ow!

284
00:10:10,877 --> 00:10:11,799
Now get me a car.

285
00:10:13,963 --> 00:10:17,298
<i>So the next day,</i>
<i>Axl put his plan into action.</i>

286
00:10:18,569 --> 00:10:21,939
So, who am I dropping off
first? (Chuckles)

287
00:10:22,050 --> 00:10:23,571
You can just drop us both
at my house.

288
00:10:23,682 --> 00:10:24,872
We're having a sleepover.

289
00:10:25,892 --> 00:10:28,378
<i>Of</i> course you are.

290
00:10:29,252 --> 00:10:30,552
(Engine starts)

291
00:10:34,428 --> 00:10:37,028
Well, I guess if everyone's here
for the mascot tryouts,

292
00:10:37,144 --> 00:10:38,542
we'll get started.

293
00:10:39,481 --> 00:10:40,635
(Indistinct conversations)

294
00:10:42,160 --> 00:10:43,150
Put on the head.

295
00:10:43,253 --> 00:10:44,457
Oh! (Laughs)

296
00:10:45,480 --> 00:10:46,193
(Exhales)

297
00:10:46,285 --> 00:10:48,482
<i>There are those moments</i>
<i>in life when the stars align</i>

298
00:10:48,595 --> 00:10:50,894
<i>and everything just</i>
<i>falls into place.</i>

299
00:10:51,043 --> 00:10:52,542
<i>And with nobody else</i>
<i>trying out,</i>

300
00:10:52,643 --> 00:10:54,326
<i>this was one</i>
<i>of those moments...</i>

301
00:10:54,448 --> 00:10:55,941
Ah! Ha ha ha!

302
00:10:56,027 --> 00:10:57,814
<i>If only Sue weren't Sue.</i>

303
00:10:57,937 --> 00:10:59,453
<i>(Man over PA)</i>
<i>Attention, students--</i>

304
00:10:59,629 --> 00:11:03,425
<i>because of low turnout, we are</i>
<i>extending mascot tryouts.</i>

305
00:11:03,669 --> 00:11:07,705
<i>Anyone is welcome.</i>
<i>Anyone. Anyone at all.</i>

306
00:11:07,812 --> 00:11:10,154
<i>Seriously. Anyone.</i>

307
00:11:11,920 --> 00:11:13,257
Brick, what are you doing?

308
00:11:13,371 --> 00:11:15,072
You're supposed to be
bonding with your bunny.

309
00:11:15,262 --> 00:11:16,667
There's something
wrong with it.

310
00:11:16,785 --> 00:11:17,965
I think it has issues.

311
00:11:18,112 --> 00:11:18,877
(High-pitched voice) Whoop.

312
00:11:18,980 --> 00:11:20,663
Come on. There's nothing
wrong with him.

313
00:11:20,776 --> 00:11:23,291
He's a sweet, soft,
cuddly bunny.

314
00:11:24,084 --> 00:11:24,964
<i>He wasn't.</i>

315
00:11:25,113 --> 00:11:26,683
(Snorts, hisses)

316
00:11:26,797 --> 00:11:28,065
(Gasps)

317
00:11:34,950 --> 00:11:37,306
<i>At first, we thought the bunny</i>
<i>was just scared of us.</i>

318
00:11:37,499 --> 00:11:38,275
Now look, Brick,

319
00:11:38,384 --> 00:11:39,600
you just gotta learn
how to handle it.

320
00:11:39,768 --> 00:11:41,052
Now you don't wanna
startle him.

321
00:11:41,236 --> 00:11:42,538
(Growls)
Aah! Son of a--

322
00:11:42,637 --> 00:11:43,239
Whoop.

323
00:11:43,361 --> 00:11:45,264
<i>And then we thought maybe</i>
<i>he was just hungry.</i>

324
00:11:45,501 --> 00:11:47,082
Well, we know
he doesn't like pop tarts,

325
00:11:47,193 --> 00:11:49,677
but he certainly has a taste
for human flesh. (Thud)

326
00:11:51,004 --> 00:11:52,686
<i>It wasn't long</i>
<i>before we realized</i>

327
00:11:52,812 --> 00:11:54,855
<i>the bunny wasn't scared of us.</i>

328
00:11:55,160 --> 00:11:56,695
<i>We were scared of him.</i>

329
00:11:56,816 --> 00:11:58,417
I am expecting
a super important phone call,

330
00:11:58,551 --> 00:11:59,855
so nobody use the phone.

331
00:11:59,990 --> 00:12:02,750
Because if nobody shows up
to try out by 5:00,

332
00:12:02,884 --> 00:12:06,196
I am the new
Thundering Hen! Aah!

333
00:12:06,325 --> 00:12:07,359
Oh, my God, it's out.
(Gasps)

334
00:12:07,479 --> 00:12:08,997
It's out of its cage!

335
00:12:09,142 --> 00:12:10,953
- Aah!
- Aah!

336
00:12:11,097 --> 00:12:11,965
Aah!

337
00:12:12,071 --> 00:12:13,141
All right! All right!
Everybody stay calm!

338
00:12:13,251 --> 00:12:13,974
I'll take care of this.

339
00:12:14,073 --> 00:12:16,799
Brick, why is the bunny loose?
It was your responsibility!

340
00:12:16,930 --> 00:12:18,831
I think you just answered
your own question.

341
00:12:18,945 --> 00:12:20,706
(Mike) - I see it!
- Aah!

342
00:12:24,637 --> 00:12:26,003
Aah!

343
00:12:26,344 --> 00:12:28,189
- Aah!
(Frankie) - There he goes!

344
00:12:28,324 --> 00:12:29,248
Sucker's fast!

345
00:12:29,540 --> 00:12:30,178
(Telephone ringing)

346
00:12:30,296 --> 00:12:32,388
(Gasps) Oh, my God!
Oh, no! That's for me!

347
00:12:32,497 --> 00:12:33,656
That's the mascot call!

348
00:12:33,767 --> 00:12:36,111
Axl, go over there and throw
me the phone! (Ringing)

349
00:12:36,195 --> 00:12:38,290
No way! I'm a football player!
I need my legs!

350
00:12:38,392 --> 00:12:39,609
Wha-- ugh!

351
00:12:39,717 --> 00:12:41,807
I see him! Right there!
Right there! Right there!

352
00:12:41,968 --> 00:12:42,916
Ooh! Ha!

353
00:12:43,901 --> 00:12:46,128
Got him cornered! Give me
something to pick him up with!

354
00:12:46,460 --> 00:12:47,689
Here, here, here, here, here.

355
00:12:50,193 --> 00:12:52,537
Damn it! Stay still,
you little rodent!

356
00:12:52,640 --> 00:12:54,368
Dad, a rabbit
is technically a mammal.

357
00:12:54,473 --> 00:12:55,365
Not now, Brick.

358
00:12:55,490 --> 00:12:57,793
- Aah! Get it! Get it!
- What do you think I'm trying to do?

359
00:12:57,957 --> 00:12:59,611
I'm coming! I'm coming!
(Ringing continues)

360
00:12:59,729 --> 00:13:01,532
Aah! Don't hang up!

361
00:13:01,985 --> 00:13:03,473
Aah! Ugh!

362
00:13:04,262 --> 00:13:05,449
(Ring)

363
00:13:06,336 --> 00:13:07,276
(Panting)

364
00:13:07,744 --> 00:13:08,128
(Ring)

365
00:13:08,238 --> 00:13:09,343
(Calmly) Hello?

366
00:13:09,445 --> 00:13:10,690
Okay, that's it.
That's it right there.

367
00:13:10,779 --> 00:13:12,251
Just grab it!
Just grab it!

368
00:13:12,397 --> 00:13:13,240
You wanna do this?

369
00:13:14,114 --> 00:13:16,873
I got it!
I'm the Thundering Hen!

370
00:13:17,146 --> 00:13:19,547
I got him!
I got the little bastard.

371
00:13:19,690 --> 00:13:20,720
Oh, yay.

372
00:13:20,820 --> 00:13:22,284
Ow, ow, ow, ow, ow
ow, ow, ow, ow!

373
00:13:22,401 --> 00:13:23,247
(Rabbit snorts and hisses)

374
00:13:23,440 --> 00:13:24,389
(Door slams)

375
00:13:26,683 --> 00:13:28,122
If you'd have just gotten
a goldfish,

376
00:13:28,250 --> 00:13:29,237
he'd be dead already.

377
00:13:31,377 --> 00:13:32,724
(Indistinct conversations)

378
00:13:33,255 --> 00:13:34,014
Hey.

379
00:13:34,175 --> 00:13:34,809
So I was thinking,

380
00:13:34,925 --> 00:13:37,355
homecoming dance might be
more fun if we double dated.

381
00:13:37,634 --> 00:13:39,882
Oh, wow, that would be fun.
Wouldn't it, Deb?

382
00:13:40,000 --> 00:13:41,865
Totally. Sounds good
to me, Court.

383
00:13:42,022 --> 00:13:44,615
Sweet. Now you wouldn't happen
to know of anyone

384
00:13:44,722 --> 00:13:46,323
who might wanna go
with my friend?

385
00:13:46,452 --> 00:13:47,785
He is really cool.

386
00:13:48,163 --> 00:13:50,844
I might know
a certain cheerleader...

387
00:13:50,962 --> 00:13:53,721
(Singsongy) who would <i>love</i>
to go with him. (Giggles)

388
00:13:55,386 --> 00:13:57,292
Sarah, we found you a date!

389
00:13:58,519 --> 00:14:00,270
You're going to
the homecoming dance with Sarah.

390
00:14:00,704 --> 00:14:02,225
Bottom-of-the-pyramid
Sarah?

391
00:14:02,398 --> 00:14:03,459
Had to be done.

392
00:14:03,629 --> 00:14:06,961
Just another casualty
in this crazy game I'm playing.

393
00:14:08,039 --> 00:14:08,943
(Exhales deeply)

394
00:14:10,776 --> 00:14:12,244
<i>Once the bunny</i>
<i>was in the bathroom,</i>

395
00:14:13,082 --> 00:14:14,393
<i>he stayed there.</i>

396
00:14:14,955 --> 00:14:16,655
<i>Kind of like Mike on a Sunday.</i>

397
00:14:17,115 --> 00:14:18,021
(Hisses)

398
00:14:23,851 --> 00:14:25,953
(Both, singsongy) Occupied.

399
00:14:31,700 --> 00:14:32,866
Okay. This is enough.

400
00:14:33,005 --> 00:14:34,825
I need to know that
I can go into my bathroom

401
00:14:34,953 --> 00:14:36,990
without hot cheerleaders
being in there.

402
00:14:37,593 --> 00:14:38,791
Yes, I'm that old.

403
00:14:39,321 --> 00:14:40,582
Bugs has gotta go.

404
00:14:40,695 --> 00:14:43,225
We can't. The stupid thing
has gotta bond with Brick.

405
00:14:43,796 --> 00:14:45,306
Brick barely bonded with me.

406
00:14:45,419 --> 00:14:47,321
He's not bonding
with psycho bunny.

407
00:14:47,458 --> 00:14:49,720
Dr. Fulton says if he can
learn to relate to the bunny,

408
00:14:49,830 --> 00:14:51,234
he can learn
to relate to people.

409
00:14:51,757 --> 00:14:52,911
Why are we making him do this?

410
00:14:53,022 --> 00:14:54,472
What's so great about people?

411
00:14:54,591 --> 00:14:56,744
Because Brick needs
to learn how to attach.

412
00:14:56,857 --> 00:14:58,833
Why? All he wants to do
is read.

413
00:14:58,948 --> 00:15:01,861
- That's not true. Brick wants to feel a
part of things. - Brick wants to whoop,

414
00:15:01,986 --> 00:15:03,261
read a book, and be left alone.

415
00:15:03,369 --> 00:15:05,319
I'm his mom. I think
I know what Brick wants.

416
00:15:05,426 --> 00:15:07,210
How do you know what Brick
wants? Have you ever asked him?

417
00:15:09,079 --> 00:15:13,328
No.
No, I have not. Wow.

418
00:15:13,542 --> 00:15:16,595
We never talk to Brick
about... anything.

419
00:15:17,308 --> 00:15:19,183
Maybe we should talk to him.

420
00:15:19,289 --> 00:15:20,216
Maybe we should.

421
00:15:20,327 --> 00:15:22,055
I mean, what's the worst
that could happen?

422
00:15:22,164 --> 00:15:23,151
He gets another tic?

423
00:15:23,429 --> 00:15:25,006
It's not like
we'd notice it, anyway.

424
00:15:25,121 --> 00:15:25,898
Yeah.

425
00:15:26,484 --> 00:15:28,500
<i>(Axl over PA)</i>
<i>Attention all students--</i>

426
00:15:28,668 --> 00:15:30,352
<i>will Axl Heck's girlfriend</i>

427
00:15:30,479 --> 00:15:32,045
<i>please report</i>
<i>to the main office.</i>

428
00:15:32,166 --> 00:15:33,061
<i>ASAP...</i>

429
00:15:33,159 --> 00:15:34,322
<i>or sooner.</i>

430
00:15:35,528 --> 00:15:37,379
I got your message, Axl.

431
00:15:37,542 --> 00:15:40,188
A crow outside my window said
you would contact me today.

432
00:15:40,401 --> 00:15:42,240
Are we going to homecoming?

433
00:15:42,347 --> 00:15:43,925
- No!
- Okay.

434
00:15:44,304 --> 00:15:45,560
See you at prom.

435
00:15:46,299 --> 00:15:48,910
(Door opens and closes)

436
00:15:51,800 --> 00:15:54,037
So, Brick, as parents,

437
00:15:54,160 --> 00:15:57,179
your dad and I often talk
about what's best for you.

438
00:15:57,347 --> 00:16:01,319
But we realize we don't always
include you in these talks.

439
00:16:02,254 --> 00:16:03,844
I appreciate your candor.

440
00:16:03,989 --> 00:16:05,713
I think I'm mature enough
to be involved.

441
00:16:05,838 --> 00:16:06,990
(High-pitched voice)
Whoop.

442
00:16:08,362 --> 00:16:10,219
So I'm just gonna
lay it out for you.

443
00:16:10,333 --> 00:16:11,242
Here goes.

444
00:16:11,647 --> 00:16:15,309
I don't think it's a secret
that you are unique,

445
00:16:15,444 --> 00:16:17,267
and we want you to stay unique.

446
00:16:17,408 --> 00:16:19,760
But not so unique
that you get labeled

447
00:16:19,875 --> 00:16:21,753
as... too unique.

448
00:16:21,883 --> 00:16:24,126
I think what we're trying
to figure out is,

449
00:16:24,321 --> 00:16:27,656
why do <i>you</i> think you have
trouble connecting with people?

450
00:16:27,781 --> 00:16:30,421
Hmm. That's
an interesting question.

451
00:16:30,620 --> 00:16:31,944
Well, I don't know.

452
00:16:32,125 --> 00:16:34,079
Could be 'cause you brought home
the wrong baby

453
00:16:34,196 --> 00:16:35,747
and I was nursed
by a strange woman.

454
00:16:35,851 --> 00:16:37,226
I mean, that might leave a scar.

455
00:16:38,000 --> 00:16:39,582
Well, Brick, you were a baby.

456
00:16:39,711 --> 00:16:41,333
- There's no way you could remember that.
- Yeah.

457
00:16:41,489 --> 00:16:43,360
Yeah. Uh-huh. That's true.

458
00:16:43,626 --> 00:16:45,332
Well, maybe it's 'cause you guys

459
00:16:45,459 --> 00:16:47,316
don't really spend
any time with me.

460
00:16:48,027 --> 00:16:49,642
We're... busy.

461
00:16:50,029 --> 00:16:52,533
And yet not too busy
to watch Dance Moms.

462
00:16:52,925 --> 00:16:54,911
Well, Brick, we're spending
time with you now,

463
00:16:55,039 --> 00:16:56,949
and you're still whooping,
so...

464
00:16:57,269 --> 00:16:59,422
I don't know.
There's just so many things.

465
00:16:59,549 --> 00:17:01,395
We never really have
any nutritious meals.

466
00:17:01,496 --> 00:17:02,547
That could be it.

467
00:17:02,670 --> 00:17:05,233
We don't have set bedtimes.
Kids need structure.

468
00:17:05,354 --> 00:17:06,873
We beg for stuff, and you cave.

469
00:17:06,969 --> 00:17:08,530
That doesn't
establish boundaries.

470
00:17:09,506 --> 00:17:11,707
Look, the point is,
you do enough weird stuff.

471
00:17:11,823 --> 00:17:13,083
You don't need another one.

472
00:17:13,591 --> 00:17:14,902
Knock off the whooping.

473
00:17:15,341 --> 00:17:16,404
The whooping?

474
00:17:16,545 --> 00:17:17,453
That's what this is about?

475
00:17:17,561 --> 00:17:18,994
I thought it was about
the other thing.

476
00:17:19,190 --> 00:17:20,361
The whispering?

477
00:17:20,551 --> 00:17:22,383
No. I have to say
the pledge of allegiance

478
00:17:22,507 --> 00:17:24,413
20 times before I go to bed.

479
00:17:24,791 --> 00:17:27,129
(Whispers)
Pledge of allegiance.

480
00:17:28,194 --> 00:17:29,410
Awesome.

481
00:17:39,752 --> 00:17:41,467
<i>Sue had finally</i>
<i>achieved her dream</i>

482
00:17:41,586 --> 00:17:43,409
<i>of becoming a Thundering Hen.</i>

483
00:17:43,605 --> 00:17:46,444
<i>And to say she was excited</i>
<i>was an understatement.</i>

484
00:17:46,978 --> 00:17:48,357
(Panting)

485
00:17:48,474 --> 00:17:49,571
<i>(Man over PA) - Ladies and gentlemen...</i>
- Aah!

486
00:17:49,687 --> 00:17:51,912
<i>...give it up</i>
<i>for your Thundering Hens!</i>

487
00:17:52,038 --> 00:17:53,999
- Hey!
- Hey! There she is!

488
00:17:54,794 --> 00:17:55,608
(Sue) Aah!

489
00:17:57,481 --> 00:17:58,398
(Crowd) Ohh!

490
00:17:58,492 --> 00:17:59,997
Oh, God, I can't look.
Did she get up?

491
00:18:00,980 --> 00:18:02,126
Yep, she popped right up.

492
00:18:02,789 --> 00:18:05,506
(Cheers and applause,
drums beating)

493
00:18:12,275 --> 00:18:15,294
- All right. There you go.
- That's the spirit. - All right!

494
00:18:17,210 --> 00:18:19,531
Wow! Good job, Sue!

495
00:18:22,679 --> 00:18:23,444
<i>It's 4th and goal</i>

496
00:18:23,551 --> 00:18:25,005
<i>with 3 seconds left</i>
<i>on the clock.</i>

497
00:18:25,112 --> 00:18:27,132
<i>The Hens gotta go</i>
<i>for the touchdown to win!</i>

498
00:18:27,269 --> 00:18:28,884
(Cheering)

499
00:18:34,140 --> 00:18:35,583
(Cheering subsides)

500
00:18:35,673 --> 00:18:37,465
<i>This was it. The final play.</i>

501
00:18:37,706 --> 00:18:39,553
<i>You could hear a pin drop.</i>

502
00:18:39,690 --> 00:18:41,038
<i>Until...</i>

503
00:18:41,141 --> 00:18:42,069
(High-pitched voice)
Whoop.

504
00:18:42,156 --> 00:18:43,435
Hey, you guys
wanna shut your kid up?

505
00:18:43,544 --> 00:18:45,417
He's been doing that
the whole game. It's annoying.

506
00:18:45,643 --> 00:18:46,903
(Mouths words)

507
00:18:47,639 --> 00:18:49,203
(Mouths words)

508
00:18:52,745 --> 00:18:54,052
Whoop!

509
00:18:54,644 --> 00:18:56,382
What? That's how we cheer.

510
00:18:56,482 --> 00:18:58,865
It's just a family thing.
It's not weird. Whoop!

511
00:19:00,566 --> 00:19:01,733
(High-pitched voice) Whoop!

512
00:19:02,064 --> 00:19:03,075
Whoop!

513
00:19:03,288 --> 00:19:03,838
Whoop!

514
00:19:04,525 --> 00:19:06,131
- Whoop!
- Whoop, whoop!

515
00:19:06,297 --> 00:19:06,892
Whoop!

516
00:19:07,052 --> 00:19:07,917
- Whoop!
- Whoop, whoop!

517
00:19:08,016 --> 00:19:09,080
Whoop!

518
00:19:09,357 --> 00:19:10,030
(Axl) Hike!

519
00:19:11,108 --> 00:19:12,817
(Cheering)

520
00:19:16,834 --> 00:19:17,814
<i>And...</i>

521
00:19:17,911 --> 00:19:18,874
<i>he's in there!</i>

522
00:19:18,988 --> 00:19:21,733
(Cheering) <i>Axl Heck has scored
the winning touchdown!</i>

523
00:19:21,842 --> 00:19:24,161
<i>The Hens have</i>
<i>pulled off a squeaker!</i>

524
00:19:24,287 --> 00:19:25,767
<i>What a great game!</i>

525
00:19:27,384 --> 00:19:28,697
There you go.

526
00:19:30,247 --> 00:19:32,251
<i>It was a great moment for Axl</i>

527
00:19:32,917 --> 00:19:35,450
<i>and an even greater moment</i>
<i>for Sue.</i>

528
00:19:36,484 --> 00:19:37,972
Yeah! (Laughs)

529
00:19:38,915 --> 00:19:40,156
<i>The only difference was,</i>

530
00:19:40,556 --> 00:19:43,995
<i>everybody knew who Axl was</i>
<i>and what he had done,</i>

531
00:19:44,183 --> 00:19:45,268
<i>but they didn't know</i>
<i>who Sue was.</i>

532
00:19:45,392 --> 00:19:46,829
Aah! (Laughs)

533
00:19:48,199 --> 00:19:50,034
<i>She was like a superhero.</i>

534
00:19:50,280 --> 00:19:53,090
<i>When she was in plainclothes,</i>
<i>she was just Sue.</i>

535
00:19:53,290 --> 00:19:54,950
<i>But when she was</i>
<i>in the mascot suit,</i>

536
00:19:55,106 --> 00:19:56,931
<i>she could do anything.</i>

537
00:19:57,493 --> 00:20:01,542
<i>Yep, so far, homecoming</i>
<i>had been a big success.</i>

538
00:20:01,669 --> 00:20:03,248
<i>But Axl still had</i>
<i>a little unfinished business.</i>

539
00:20:03,391 --> 00:20:04,130
(Clears throat)

540
00:20:04,259 --> 00:20:06,880
Okay. Here's the corsage
right here.

541
00:20:06,991 --> 00:20:10,082
So come and get it... you.

542
00:20:10,191 --> 00:20:11,241
A wrist corsage?

543
00:20:11,358 --> 00:20:12,753
Oh. We don't wear those.

544
00:20:12,855 --> 00:20:14,717
We don't. They leave
marks on your wrists.

545
00:20:14,825 --> 00:20:16,801
- He's so sweet, though.
- Isn't he?

546
00:20:17,665 --> 00:20:19,419
(Indistinct conversations)
(Thud)

547
00:20:19,799 --> 00:20:21,515
<i>♪</i>

548
00:20:21,638 --> 00:20:22,585
(Exhales deeply)

549
00:20:23,842 --> 00:20:26,977
Well?
Man, you still don't know?

550
00:20:27,114 --> 00:20:29,168
You better hurry. We're about
to leave for the dance.

551
00:20:29,276 --> 00:20:31,891
That's it. I'm just
going for it and picking one.

552
00:20:32,264 --> 00:20:35,530
I got a 60/40 chance, so, uh...

553
00:20:35,955 --> 00:20:37,051
Courtney!

554
00:20:41,692 --> 00:20:42,848
Axl!

555
00:20:43,935 --> 00:20:44,532
Ow.

556
00:20:44,684 --> 00:20:45,684
(Murmuring)

557
00:20:46,084 --> 00:20:47,023
Uh...

558
00:20:47,270 --> 00:20:48,328
Debbie!

559
00:20:49,736 --> 00:20:50,819
Ooh.

560
00:20:51,343 --> 00:20:52,163
<i>What?</i>

561
00:20:52,269 --> 00:20:53,800
That was totally inappropriate.

562
00:20:53,920 --> 00:20:54,916
Totally.

563
00:20:55,251 --> 00:20:56,265
Hold on. Why are you mad?

564
00:20:56,374 --> 00:20:57,385
'Cause you're
my girlfriend's best friend,

565
00:20:57,484 --> 00:20:59,216
or because you're my girlfriend,
and I kissed you inappropriately

566
00:20:59,303 --> 00:21:00,486
in front of your best friend?

567
00:21:00,603 --> 00:21:02,525
Wait! Don't go!

568
00:21:02,601 --> 00:21:04,919
One of you
is really important to me!

569
00:21:08,483 --> 00:21:11,113
<i>So the bunny didn't exactly</i>
<i>fix Brick,</i>

570
00:21:11,327 --> 00:21:12,895
<i>but it did bring us</i>
<i>closer together</i>

571
00:21:12,997 --> 00:21:14,959
<i>in a way we never expected.</i>

572
00:21:16,475 --> 00:21:18,482
The thing is, life is messy,

573
00:21:18,584 --> 00:21:19,945
<i>but you gotta keep trying.</i>

574
00:21:20,118 --> 00:21:21,554
Look, I'm just really into you,

575
00:21:21,640 --> 00:21:23,364
and I think it'd be awesome
to get back together.

576
00:21:23,457 --> 00:21:25,057
Or go out for the first time.

577
00:21:26,092 --> 00:21:27,060
Hello?

578
00:21:27,807 --> 00:21:28,901
Hello?

579
00:21:29,282 --> 00:21:31,501
<i>It's a multipronged approach.</i>

580
00:21:37,565 --> 00:21:42,893
Sync and corrections by n17t01
